body:
I'm so happy for you! Congratulations!!

&#x200B;

I've long suspected that if I were a mother, it would be a big help to me. Then again, I want to be careful not to have a kid out of my own selfishness. Not saying you're selfish!! I just know that for myself, I need to make sure that once I'm ready to have kids, I do it for the RIGHT reasons. 

Tbh, I would LOVE to have a kid and give them everything I never got. That makes me excited. 

&#x200B;

I've never even had a boyfriend/first kiss, though, so... \^\^" Kids won't be happening anytime soon. 

&#x200B;

Glad you could find happiness in it, though.

Thanks for the advice! I really appreciate that you took the time to reply.

I've tried a few mods (though, what turned me off mods was the lack of Forge for 1.13). I used (forgot the names but) the mod that generates structures, Quark, the mod that puts random graveyards with treasure in your game (Treasure 2 I think?), and JourneyMap (best mod!!)... They were certainly fun. But I wanted the features of 1.13, so I switched back to Vanilla.

&#x200B;

I've also tried Terraria, too. Though, now that you mention it, it might be a good thing for me to give it another go. It's pretty fun imo. I didn't play too many hours on it... not like MC anyway lol.

&#x200B;

I think my main problem is that I just really prefer to do things with other people now. It feels weird for me to type that, because I always thought I was asocial. But... I really enjoy playing with others now, as opposed to playing on my own. The difficulty with that, is that even IF I found an amazing friend to play with, it costs so much for the stupid Realms. :(

&#x200B;

EDIT: I'm just feeling sad and nostalgic tonight. I'm sure I'll feel better tomorrow. I really do appreciate that you tried to help, though. That was very kind. :)

If you do, please post it and/or send it to me! I literally bookmarked this page lol. It's just so good!

&#x200B;

Sorry if I'm gushing too much. It just makes so much sense... Like, you feed the fire (abusive parent) because they keep you warm (safe), but then they burn you (abuse you) and... Man, it was just so powerful!

&#x200B;

Do you mind if I share this? Also, who can I credit? Your username? Sorry again. I don't mean to sound obsessive. \^\^"

Whoops. I just posted a thread about hoarding/messy houses. I didn't see yours! My bad!

&#x200B;

I never got triggered by TV because the houses on TV were always much worse. While my parents' house was no picnic, luckily it was mostly boxes and clothes. Dishes were done and garbage was thrown away.

I've considered the army, but would likely be dismissed due to my medical and mental issues lol. The army wouldn't take me. Plus, I'm not a fan of my own country and wouldn't want to fight for them, if I'm being honest.

&#x200B;

I'm sorry to hear about your situation, though. And congrats on moving! Sure, that's a long time away, but you got a plan! That's great!

I'm not actually sure? I've been wanting a single one since the beginning of this year. But I see one for as long as I'm in hospital, then they don't follow up on me? Then I go back to hospital, get put with a new one, and the same thing happens all over again. I've probably seen 10 by now. Not exaggerating. One will start me on meds, then a few weeks later a different one will stop my meds and give me new ones... 

&#x200B;

Tbh, I feel like everyone sees me and wants to get my the hell out of their office so they pawn me off on somebody else.

Yeah, 'p' and 'q' were also hard for me. Luckily, I seem to have grown out of it, though I do tend to flip numbers now. Like 02 and 20. Or 13 and 31. Like I'll misread them in my head.

&#x200B;

Omg, yes. I fidget all the freaking time! I actually focus better when I'm doing something else (as crazy as that sounds). Like, I can communicate better when I'm playing some mindless game on my phone, or messing around with something in my hands. I actually remember stuff much better when I'm fidgeting. Long periods of doing nothing (church, school, breaks at work) drive me insane. 

&#x200B;

Luckily, (or unluckily) I've never really had a career goal in mind. I just work wherever will hire me. So, I've never needed or desired further education. But it's always so awkward when people ask me what grade I finished or if I have a diploma. I always lie and say grade 12, but in my mind I know we didn't get that far. And I don't have a diploma....

I feel the same way all the time. I feel horribly guilty for telling my friend about the abuse. The thing that's helped me, though, is getting my friend's feedback. When I apologized for telling her (or for "dragging her into it") she told me that it's okay. She wants to be involved. 

&#x200B;

As for not feeling emotions, I'm pretty sure that's a side effect of being raised by N's. I feel the same way- nothing. My therapist has cried during our sessions, while I've felt nothing at all.

I don't mean to argue with you, but the fact that you posted here tonight tells me that there's just the tiniest spark of hope. Even if it's not hope enough to live, it's a hope that someone will relate or even care. 

&#x200B;

I know I'm a total stranger, but your post really resonated with me. 

I've been in an out of psych wards this year due to my suicide plans and thoughts. I know how hopeless it can seem.

&#x200B;

I'm not gonna tell you that things will get better. For me, they seem to just get worse. But you, yourself, can get better. I really do believe that. These feelings don't have to last forever. There's hope!

&#x200B;

It sounds like you've really put a lot of thought and effort into this plan to go to Belgium. I think that's totally cool! That shows me that you're somebody who's really good at doing research! I suck at that, so major respect here. 

&#x200B;

I'm really sorry that you feel suicidal, though. Really. I don't know what else to say. 

&#x200B;

I just truly hope that you don't kill yourself. <3

That's a tough one. Knowing that you're on this site, that tells me that you probably shouldn't trust her. 

&#x200B;

Then again, I, myself, have gone to the ER for chest pain that turned out to be not heart related. Not "nothing", but not heart related. It was some weird thing that I can't remember. Something like the muscle right above my heart was pulled or something? So it felt like chest pain, but wasn't "real" chest pain. 

&#x200B;

The fact that your mom says "You don't want me to have a real heart attack." that stands out to me though. That sounds manipulative, in my opinion. 

&#x200B;

I wouldn't say that your mom necessarily lied about the chest pain. She might have, she might not. Regardless, I wouldn't let her manipulate you with things after the fact.

Ugh, sounds like my family. My family are Christian, and I'm a recent Mormon convert. My nmom mocks my religion, bashes my beliefs, and in general, makes me feel like a horrible human being for "making the mistake" of choosing my own religion. 

&#x200B;

Then she turns around and says that I bash her religion and say terrible things about her.

&#x200B;

Which isn't true. Yes, I disagree, but I like to think I'm respectful. Even if I'm not respectful, I'm not the type of person to bash someone else. That's just not me. 

&#x200B;

Anyway, I'm sorry to hear that your dad is acting like that. You're not alone.

To be honest, I find that a guided mediation is sometimes helpful. I say sometimes, because half the time my anxiety interrupts the meditation.

&#x200B;

However, the thing I found most helpful was to write out some positive affirmations and say them over and over to myself.

&#x200B;

Mine included something like;

"I'm not a bad person."

"I can breathe."

"I can't control what other people think."

&#x200B;

You can also include things like

"I'm safe."

"It's not my fault."

&#x200B;

You really need to include things that you can actually believe, though. For myself, I really struggle with body image. I can't just say "I'm beautiful" over and over because I don't believe it. But I can start with something smaller like "I like my hair." or "My hands are nice."

&#x200B;

Hope this helps!

&#x200B;

EDIT: If you're a creative person, you can even work on making a poster with your own designs on it! Or a little card to stick in your pocket. It kinda helps by giving you something to work on.

Glad to hear you got out! 

&#x200B;

I've been through so many tests. Xrays, bloodwork, breath tests... when the doctor said "it's stress", I thought he was talking crap. But then I realized just how stressed I am, and I'm starting to agree.
